-- Task unwitnessed-gaussian-let-chain-admitted-but-crashes: the repro shape.
-- 'x' is unwitnessed (its only occurrence is an operand of a plus whose other
-- operand is fresh), so no inference engine could reach it and the set-witness
-- refusal killed the whole compile -- generate included. SPLL.Typing.LetInline
-- substitutes the single-use binding away, so the inline Gaussian shortcut sees
-- Normal + Normal and answers N(0, 2).
main = let x = Normal in let y = x + Normal in y
